welcome back to the David Pakman show  I'm fair and cousins from Ring of Fire  sitting in for David Pakman today and I  will also be with you tomorrow you know  a lot has been said recently about guns  in the United States obviously for very  good reasons there's a huge movement  we've got to get some kind of gun  control but there's there's another  issue related to that that we absolutely  also have to discuss and it is the fact  that right now the United States  Department of Defense the United States  military is spending money at such an  alarming rate that you have to wonder  what is on the horizon according to a  recent report Lockheed Martin in 2017  got thirty five point two billion  dollars from the US Defense Department  they accounted that money to Lockheed  Martin from the Defense Department  accounted for 70 percent of the  company's total sales in 2017 that  thirty five billion dollars is more than  the United States funded NASA with last  year it's the same as the GDP of Bolivia  according to reports and that's how much  we spent on just one defense contractor  to buy their fighter jets Boeing not too  far behind them got twenty six point  five billion in 2016 and excuse me the  Lockheed Martin money was 2016 not 2017  but look we are spending tens of  billions of dollars per defense  contractor right now we just upped the  military budget for this coming year  more billions upon billions upon  billions to feed this disgusting war  machine that we have built as a country  but this 35 billion to Lockheed Martin  alone not even including the twenty six  billion the Boeing  this is disgusting for the United States  for many many reasons first and foremost  because we've been told a little too  often in the last year that as a country  we simply can't afford something as as  monumental as universal health care we  can't afford debt-free college we can't  afford to forgive student loans anymore  why well for one because we've got to  get tax cuts to our wealthy donors but  two because these poor defense  contractors are just starving for our  money I think about that if we just took  only the money that we gave to Lockheed  and Boeing in a single year which is  more than sixty billion dollars because  that's a 35-point to two Lockheed is  actually a little bit lower than usual  their average is about 38 billion a year  so anyway just those two Lockheed and  Boeing 60 billion a year how many  doctors visits could that buy for  American citizens how many prescriptions  could that fill how many cancer  screenings could that fund how many  students could we send to college how  many school lunches could we buy for  starving American children how many  homes could we build for the homeless I  mean the possibilities of what we could  do with this money are endless but  instead we're buying tanks  we're buying long-range missiles that  was part of this thirty-five billion  dollars that Lockheed got was because  we're currently having several different  companies develop new long-range  missiles and it's basically a bidding  war we're giving each company that makes  these things some money to develop one  and whoever makes the best one is going  to get the main contract to get billions  upon billions more according to the  Washington Post so essentially we're  having a bidding war right now to see  who can make the bomb that goes the  farthest and blows up the most things  and then whoever gets that whoever makes  it whoever creates it you're gonna get a  few extra billion dollars because  congratulations you won the American  contest of death because let's be honest  that's what this is that's what is  happening here we are so invested the  military complex here in the United  States is so invested in destroying as  much as possible that the government  doesn't care what they're blowing money  on meanwhile too many kids in this  country go each day without enough to  eat they're not getting proper nutrition  we have US military veterans and other  American citizens that sleep on the  streets each night they don't know where  their next meal is going to come from  they don't have a roof over their head  if it gets too cold they freeze to death  if it gets too hot they can die from  dehydration and yet we're dumping tens  of billions of dollars into each  individual defense contractor and that's  what's disgusting here this isn't all of  them as a whole this is what we give  each individual one students right now  who are saying I can't go to college  because one I can't afford it and two I  can't afford to be straddled with that  hundred thousand dollars in student loan  debt for the next 40 years of my life so  they don't go meanwhile 35 billion to  Lockheed 26 billion to Boeing in one  single year and you're gonna sit there  and tell me that we can't get universal  health care that we can't get debt-free  college that we can't address the issue  of homelessness that we can't not cut  Social Security and Medicare and  Medicaid and all of these other programs  designed to help American citizens why  because we need to go blow more stuff up  because we need to just show our  military might because Donald Trump  needs a few more floats for his parade  is that what this is about something has  to change  cannot continue on as a country when we  think that it's more important to build  up our arsenal of tanks and planes and  bombs just in case because let's never  forget the United States military is  better funded than any other military on  the planet as a percentage of GDP we pay  more spend more on our military then  most of the rest of the industrialized  world combined not just more but more  combined than most of them we could cut  our military budget almost in half and  still be spending more than any other  country in the world on our military and  yet when it comes to taking care of our  citizens  we're among the last among the  industrialized world

